The independent register uses the exact TOML layout below as its unserved draft, not as an artifact. Keys, table names, rows, order, string spellings, LF/UTF-8/no-BOM and the single final LF are fixed as printed. The empty argument/default arrays mean exactly no arguments/defaults, not unknown metadata. The string not-applicable means the property cannot occur in this edition for the stated reason; not-yet-admitted means required evidence is still owed and always prevents served execution. Neither means zero or unlimited. Each pending weight or ceiling is replaced, in its owning measurement cut, by an inline table containing status = "admitted", value = a positive integer and unit = the unit fixed here, in that key order; the pending spelling is never published at the register coordinate. The printed layout includes decoding_work; completion admits values in these rows and adds no further row without a new design decision before the first generation. The final source is reviewed and compared as bytes before its first generation, so the draft-to-completed change is not an artifact succession. A TOML reader rejects duplicate or unknown keys/tables, missing keys, reordered or extra semantic rows, wrong types, inconsistent status/value combinations and unknown status/failure/unit spellings before agreement; accepting unknown extension keys or coercing pending values is set aside because it conceals disagreement. The independent agreement check compares operation, argument and result shapes and the closed failure mapping, then requires every applicable ceiling and weight admitted before served execution. The completed-register agreement additionally requires resolver_work to be at least the declared work_weights charge for one start before generation or served construction, so its sole operation is not statically excluded by its own budget. A smaller ceiling refuses completed-register agreement without inventing or increasing either value; the register-building cut owns this comparison and its below/equal/above controls. Explicit unserved request-limit fixtures may still choose a smaller resolver_work to witness refusal and do not admit an edition; this condition promises cost admissibility, not readiness or immunity to other refusals. The draft parser may accept pending values only in its explicit unserved agreement/measurement mode, which no served bootstrap input can select.

